Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::a_shutdown_notification_changes_only_its_field`.

The defect: `shutdown_controller_configuration` sets bit 14 without clearing the Shutdown
Notification field first. From a running configuration (the field at 00b) it still writes 01b and
passes, but over a word that carries an earlier abrupt notification (10b) it writes 11b, a value
the specification reserves, and the controller may ignore the notification and never flush its
cache.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!((shutdown >> 14) & 0b11, 0b01)`.

diff --git a/src/configuration.rs b/src/configuration.rs
--- a/src/configuration.rs
+++ b/src/configuration.rs
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@
 #[doc(alias = "CC.SHN")]
 #[doc(alias = "SHN")]
 pub fn shutdown_controller_configuration(configuration: u32) -> u32 {
-    (configuration & !(0b11 << 14)) | 0b01 << 14
+    configuration | 0b01 << 14
 }
 
